     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #e1e1e1 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Javier Santos<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, June 21, 2017 11:26 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Reconstruction of missing LMs using geometric reflection<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hi All,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I want to compare in mouse crania the reconstruction of missing data between the TPS method and that of geometric reflection.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">The estimate.missing() function seems to be working perfectly, however there can&#39;t be blank spaces between specimens in the .tps file. It could be interesting to mention this in the help section\r\n of the function.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">On the other hand, I am having trouble understanding the geometric reflection as explained in Claude (2008), and I was hoping maybe someone could help me out.  I&#39;m attaching the code and the .tps\r\n file for one individual with one missing 3D LM. I am lost on how to recover the coordinates for the missing LM... the code is working though, I think I just don&#39;t know how to interpret what to do after the eigenrotation.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Any help would be appreciated, thanks!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Best wishes,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Javier<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
